From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arsslen Idadi <arsslens021@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:05:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] pam: Take fprintd's signals from its own connection only

Once fprintd is running, ask the bus which connection owns
net.reactivated.Fprint and match its signals on that connection's
unique name, and have each handler ignore a message whose sender is
another one. NameOwnerChanged counts only when the bus itself sent it.
If the owner cannot be found, fingerprint authentication is unavailable
and the stack goes on to the next module.
---
 pam/pam_fprintd.c             |  66 ++++++++++++++++++-
 tests/pam/test_pam_fprintd.py | 120 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 183 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

